---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# The unwrapping twin of `505-distill-state-item-cast` (#996). Its header
# carries the whole argument: a distinct()/skip()-led stateful distill erases
# the element type, so it runs on `bridge-input ↦ Ljava/lang/Object;`, `512`
# loads the item with a fixed `aload 1`, `503` frames it as Object, and the
# first body opcode that wants a NARROWER reference is rejected — "Bad type on
# operand stack: Type 'java/lang/Object' is not assignable to
# 'java/lang/Integer'". `505` splices the `checkcast` in front of that opcode,
# where the item is first needed and after the frame that rightly still says
# Object.
#
# `505` anchors on an `invokestatic` onto a desugared `lambda$` wrapper and
# takes the wrapper from the call's first ARGUMENT. An unwrapping call is the
# other shape with the same problem and neither half of that recipe: it is an
# `invokevirtual`, and the type it needs is its RECEIVER — `Integer.intValue()`
# takes no argument at all. `246-transform-object-to-primitive-after-stateful`
# mints exactly such a call directly behind a distinct or a skip inside `212`'s
# boxing sandwich, so `IntStream.distinct().mapToObj(Integer::toString)` lands
# on it: the guard hands the Object on, `intValue` wants an Integer, and
# nothing in between narrows it.
#
# The `when` keeps this to a genuine unwrapping — a no-argument call returning
# a primitive, onto a class that is not java/lang/Object — so an ordinary
# no-argument object method riding the same position is left alone, and the
# cast can never be minted onto Object itself. Everything else, including the
# fixpoint argument for why the spliced cast does not re-match (it breaks the
# frame → invoke adjacency this rule anchors on), is `505`'s.
name: distill-state-item-cast-unbox
pattern: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.distill-lambda,
    static ↦ 𝑒-static,
    bridge-input ↦ "Ljava/lang/Object;",
    consumer ↦ 𝑒-consumer,
    target-method ↦ 𝑒-target-method,
    captured ↦ 𝑒-captured,
    body ↦ ⟦
      𝐵-before,
      𝜏-frame ↦ ⟦ φ ↦ Φ.jeo.frame, 𝐵-frame-rest ⟧,
      𝜏-invoke ↦ ⟦
        φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokevirtual,
        i2 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-class,
        i3 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-method,
        i4 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-signature,
        i5 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-is-interface
      ⟧,
      𝐵-after
    ⟧
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.distill-lambda,
    static ↦ 𝑒-static,
    bridge-input ↦ "Ljava/lang/Object;",
    consumer ↦ 𝑒-consumer,
    target-method ↦ 𝑒-target-method,
    captured ↦ 𝑒-captured,
    body ↦ ⟦
      𝐵-before,
      𝜏-frame ↦ ⟦ φ ↦ Φ.jeo.frame, 𝐵-frame-rest ⟧,
      𝜏-cast ↦ ⟦ φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.checkcast, i1 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-class ⟧,
      𝜏-invoke ↦ ⟦
        φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokevirtual,
        i2 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-class,
        i3 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-method,
        i4 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-signature,
        i5 ↦ 𝑒-invoke-is-interface
      ⟧,
      𝐵-after
    ⟧
  ⟧
when:
  and:
    - matches: ['^\(\)[BCDFIJSZ]$', 𝑒-invoke-signature]
    - not:
        eq: [𝑒-invoke-class, '"java/lang/Object"']
where:
  - meta: 𝜏-cast
    function: random-tau
